1
00:00:06,860 --> 00:00:11,510
Adult tickets cost A dollars, and child tickets cost C dollars.

2
00:00:11,560 --> 00:00:18,250
A family buys 2 adult tickets and 3 child tickets, and pays with a 100 dollar note.

3
00:00:18,300 --> 00:00:22,200
Is the change 100 minus, bracket, 2A plus 3C?

4
00:00:22,250 --> 00:00:24,300
Or 100 minus 2A plus 3C?

5
00:00:24,350 --> 00:00:28,060
Pause the video and choose.

6
00:00:28,110 --> 00:00:30,430
The whole cost is 2A plus 3C.

7
00:00:30,480 --> 00:00:38,800
The change takes all of it away from 100, so it needs a bracket: 100 minus, bracket, 2A plus 3C.

8
00:00:38,850 --> 00:00:41,900
Remember: collect like terms to simplify.

9
00:00:41,950 --> 00:00:45,250
3 X plus 2 Y minus X is 2 X plus 2 Y.

10
00:00:45,300 --> 00:00:47,660
Turn each phrase into an operation.

11
00:00:47,710 --> 00:00:53,090
Use a bracket when a whole quantity is multiplied, divided, or squared.

12
00:00:53,140 --> 00:00:53,760
Your turn.

13
00:00:53,810 --> 00:00:56,710
Write an expression for the mean of A and B.

14
00:00:56,760 --> 00:00:59,920
Pause the video and try it.

15
00:00:59,970 --> 00:01:02,910
Add them, then divide by how many there are.

16
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:08,010
The mean of two numbers is their total, in a bracket, divided by 2.

17
00:01:08,060 --> 00:01:12,700
Always say what the letters stand for, and check with a number.

18
00:01:12,750 --> 00:01:14,040
Here is the method.

19
00:01:14,090 --> 00:01:19,120
Step 1: choose letters for the unknowns, and say what they mean.

20
00:01:19,170 --> 00:01:22,830
Step 2: turn each phrase into an operation.

21
00:01:22,880 --> 00:01:27,720
Step 3: use brackets for a total, or a sum, that is operated on.

22
00:01:27,770 --> 00:01:31,670
Step 4: simplify, then test with a simple number.

23
00:01:31,720 --> 00:01:32,990
Ali is X years old.

24
00:01:33,040 --> 00:01:37,640
His sister is 3 years younger, and his father is 4 times Ali's age.

25
00:01:37,690 --> 00:01:40,270
Write the total of their ages.

26
00:01:40,320 --> 00:01:42,410
X, plus X minus 3, plus 4 X.

27
00:01:42,460 --> 00:01:45,400
Collect like terms: 6 X minus 3.

28
00:01:45,450 --> 00:01:48,460
A rectangle has sides of X plus 4, and 2 X.

29
00:01:48,510 --> 00:01:51,420
Its perimeter is two of each side.

30
00:01:51,470 --> 00:01:52,120
Your turn.

31
00:01:52,170 --> 00:01:54,690
Write the perimeter, and simplify it.

32
00:01:54,740 --> 00:01:57,620
Pause and work it out.

33
00:01:57,670 --> 00:02:00,430
2 lots of X plus 4 is 2 X plus 8.

34
00:02:00,480 --> 00:02:02,220
2 lots of 2 X is 4 X.

35
00:02:02,270 --> 00:02:04,730
Altogether, 6 X plus 8.

36
00:02:04,780 --> 00:02:06,490
Test with X equals 1.

37
00:02:06,540 --> 00:02:10,350
The sides are 5 and 2, so the perimeter is 14.

38
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:11,950
And 6 plus 8 is 14.

39
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:13,250
It works.

40
00:02:13,300 --> 00:02:16,750
A price of P dollars goes up by 15 percent.

41
00:02:16,800 --> 00:02:21,450
The multiplier is 1.15, so the new price is 1.15 P.

42
00:02:21,500 --> 00:02:24,670
Ben writes: the total of A and B, divided by 4.

43
00:02:24,720 --> 00:02:26,580
Which line is wrong?

44
00:02:26,630 --> 00:02:27,760
Line 1 is wrong.

45
00:02:27,810 --> 00:02:29,900
Only B would be divided by 4.

46
00:02:29,950 --> 00:02:32,370
The total needs a bracket.

47
00:02:32,420 --> 00:02:36,530
It should be the bracket A plus B, all divided by 4.

48
00:02:36,580 --> 00:02:40,660
Online shops build expressions to price your basket.

49
00:02:40,710 --> 00:02:49,550
10 percent off 2 adult and 3 child tickets, plus 5 dollars delivery, is 0.9, bracket, 2A plus 3C, plus 5.

50
00:02:49,600 --> 00:02:50,850
One last question.

51
00:02:50,900 --> 00:02:54,410
Write an expression for 20 percent off a price P.

52
00:02:54,460 --> 00:02:57,770
Pause the video and answer.

53
00:02:57,820 --> 00:03:00,660
20 percent off leaves 80 percent.

54
00:03:00,710 --> 00:03:03,480
So the new price is 0.8 P.

55
00:03:03,530 --> 00:03:07,110
To remember: say what your letters stand for.

56
00:03:07,160 --> 00:03:10,080
Use brackets for whole quantities.

57
00:03:10,130 --> 00:03:13,110
Simplify by collecting like terms.

58
00:03:13,160 --> 00:03:16,170
Test your expression with a number.

59
00:03:16,220 --> 00:03:21,390
Great work! Now practise lesson 2.2 on Camday.
